.TH elfshaker-list-packs 1  "elfshaker 1.0.0-rc1" "elfshaker Manual"
.SH NAME
elfshaker\-list\-packs \- List pack indexes known to the data directory.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBelfshaker list\-packs\fR [\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-data\-dir\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Lists local, loose, and remote pack indexes known to the data directory. Output lines are sorted.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR [default: %p]
Pretty\-print each result using placeholders:
.RS 4
\fB%p\fR \- pack
.br
\fB%h\fR \- human\-readable size
.br
\fB%b\fR \- size in bytes
.br
\fB%c\fR \- number of snapshots
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-verbose\fR
Show informational progress and diagnostic messages.
.TP
\fB\-\-data\-dir\fR \fI<PATH>\fR [default: elfshaker_data]
Use PATH as the data directory containing packs, indexes, loose objects, remotes, and HEAD. This does not change the working directory.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
